#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# order

#% text
# `order(a, b)` gives 1 when `a` comes before `b` in the canonical order, -1 when it comes after, and 0 when they are the same term. Ordering functions like it can be given to `sort` and `is_ordered`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
order(1, 2)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
order(b, a)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
order(x, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
sort([3, 1, 2], order)
#% output
#= [1, 2, 3]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sort`, `is_ordered`, `numerical_order`, `alphabetic_order`, `lexicographic_order`
